## .dive-ci — image-size + layer-efficiency budget enforced in CI.
##
## Loaded by `dive --ci <image>` in .github/workflows/docker-size-budget.yml.
## Runs after every Dockerfile / dependency change and fails the PR if any
## of the rules below fire — catches accidental image bloat at PR time
## instead of after a year of slow drift.
##
## Tuning notes:
##   - Numbers were calibrated against the Tier-1-pruned api image (806 MB)
##     and the Next.js standalone web image (348 MB). Bumps are explicit
##     and reviewable here, not silent.
##   - lowestEfficiency is a 0–1 ratio of "useful bytes" (i.e. files that
##     actually survive into the final image) over total bytes added across
##     all layers. < 0.95 typically means a layer added something a later
##     layer deleted — pure dead weight.
##   - highestUserWastedPercent is the fraction of the image that is dead
##     weight. > 0.05 = > 5% of the image is wasted bytes.
##   - highestWastedBytes is the absolute cap. 50 MB feels generous; tune
##     downward as the image gets leaner.

rules:
  # Fail if image-stack efficiency drops below 95%.
  lowestEfficiency: 0.95

  # Fail if more than 5% of total image bytes are "wasted" (added by one
  # layer and removed by a later one).
  highestUserWastedPercent: 0.05

  # Hard cap on absolute wasted bytes — 50 MB.
  highestWastedBytes: 50000000
